I suppose that a spell of trap creation would make more sense.  It would be
subject to the usage limitations of spells and so on.  I guess I'm just
enchanted ;-) with engravings.  How about using the spell to create the
trap, with some traps created out of object piles (arrows, darts, scrolls of
teleport, etc.) and some of the more magical traps optionally created by
using the spell on an engraving.  As for inappropriate stuff, it should be
unaffected - after all we need to "bait" the trap!

Meanwhile..
In article <36667@cornell.UUCP> ryan@svax.cs.cornell.edu (Ryan Borgstrom) writes:
>3) Having more engravings would certainly improve the game; you could have 
>to discover them in a similar manner to scroll names (as in, you can't write
>a genocide scroll 'till you've seen one; can't scribe Elbereth until you've 
>met with an elf, and so forth). 

I really agree with this point.  BTW, I still think that being able to create
an altar by blessing an engraving (once you know the word) would be a nice
enhancement.

A general comment: IMHO the "best" added features to Nethack are those that
use existing verbs and existing objects in new ways.  I guess thats why I
am so hung up on getting more "use" out of engravings.

More engraving ideas:

1) An engraving of a pentagram (how would this be specified?).
   Stand inside and be safe from demons and were-monsters.
   (Obviously this assumes that Elbereth is made harder to engrave.)
   Now this could also be used to trap a demon - but the demon would
   have to be generated inside it.

2) Somewhere in the dungeon, the notes for the castle door might be
   engraved.  Other random engravings that the lucky explorer might
   find would be ready-to-enchant engravings to make traps.  This would
   then be one way to learn the appropriate words to engrave.   Of
   course you wouldn't know in advance what sort of trap you were
   going to create...

3) An engraving of enlightenment.  You stare at the engraving by doing
   the ":" command three times in a row.  All of a sudden, you gain
   insight (like a potion of self-enlightenment).  It would have a
   chance of fading each time you did this.

Other possible engravings could grant telepathy (while standing on it),
or other powers of detection.   I dunno, am I wandering off here?
I think the idea of engraving/blessing an altar is the best of the lot.



